Week of Mar 16. 11 cases in, 10 closed, 1 open (S3). Median first response 36 min, median close 4.8 h. No S1/S2. Quietest week since January; nothing for anyone outside support.

By customer:
- Northstar (4): Rosa Jimenez's planners, pre-training questions on the shift board (filters, the two-plant-code view). All closed same day; I've handed the recurring ones to Hana for the training deck. Rosa: "we'll stop asking after Tuesday, promise."
- Coastline (3): steps to pin the export column order (closed, CS-2263), one "Failed" export that was their ERP being down for maintenance, which is exactly what the new state is for (closed), one password reset.
- Halberd (2): one password reset; one question from a Line 1 supervisor about the (x4) grouping in SMS ("is this new?" - yes; closed with the release note).
- Veritas (0): nothing this week.
- Other (2): one Pinewood scheduler asking whether the help center applies to pilots (yes), one spam.

Open (S3):
- CS-2268 Coastline: audit log export beta returns the proxy IP for SSO users. Known, footnoted in the release notes; Felix has a follow-up ticket. Customer is fine with it.

Trend: export-related cases down again; scheduler retries removed the "it didn't run" category entirely this week.

